Please note: The problem description "If the return value is negative, "last index of x in old array" is -1" can be misleading. It says that the return value of `LastIndexOf` method is -1; however, in a collection (like ArrayList), `LastIndexOf` method returns -1 if the element does not exist. So, the result of -1 means "the element does not exist in the list", not "the last index of the element in the list was -1".--------------------This is a C# code that uses Debug.Assert statements to verify the code conditions. It asserts that the changes in the array list count have not changed, the index of x in the array list has not increased, the last index of x in the array list has not decreased, the array list doesn't contain x and that if the return value is negative, the last index of x in the old array is -1.

Please note that these assertions are dependent on the behavior that you expect your testing harness to execute and does not validate if the actual array list operations are working as expected.
The code also only checks for integer type and does not factor in complex objects or other cases.

```cs
using System;

[TestFixture, PexClass]
public partial class ArrayListContractTest
{
    [PexMethod]
    public void PUT_AddContract([PexAssumeUnderTest]ArrayList arrList, int x)
    {
        AssumePrecondition.IsTrue(true);

        int Old_arrListCount = arrList.Count;
        int Old_x = x;
        int Old_arrListIndexOfX = arrList.IndexOf(x);
        int Old_arrListLastIndexOfX = arrList.LastIndexOf(x);
        bool Old_arrListContainsX = arrList.Contains(x);

        int New_Ret = arrList.Add(x);

        int New_arrListCount = arrList.Count;
        int New_arrListIndexOfX = arrList.IndexOf(x);
        int New_arrListLastIndexOfX = arrList.LastIndexOf(x);

        bool New_arrListContainsX = arrList.Contains(x);

        Assert.AreEqual(Old_arrListCount, New_arrListCount, "Count does not have the same value after adding.");
        Assert.LessOrEqual(Old_arrListIndexOfX, New_arrListIndexOfX, "Index of x has increased.");
        Assert.GreaterOrEqual(Old_arrListLastIndexOfX, New_arrListLastIndexOfX, "Last index of x is decreased.");
        Assert.IsFalse(New_arrListContainsX, "Collection should not contain x.");
        if (New_Ret < 0)
        {
            Assert.AreEqual(-1, Old_arrListLastIndexOfX, "Last index of x in old list should be -1.");
        }

    }
    // Similarly, other PUT_* methods are added as per the requirements.
}
```

Note: This is a direct translation of the comments, but some details may not be 1-to-1 due to various constraints around the codebase. If there are any inconsistencies, please refer to the original comments for clarifications.--------------------